    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d398-a4">

                <pb facs="0596" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg502"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No.
                    285.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Unterberger to Mr. Breckinridge.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-04-05"><hi rendition="#italic">April 5/17,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 70.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: Concerning your letter of the
                    3/15th April, I have the honor to inform you that it is much easier for me to
                    call upon you for a conversation about the mentioned case. Therefore, I propose,
                    with your permission, to pay a visit to your excellency next Wednesday, the
                    10/22 April, at 11 o’clock in the morning.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. Unterberger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
